      <h2>Cross-government health creation</h2>
      <p>
        Health is shaped far more by decisions made outside the Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC) than within it. To build a healthier UK, national Arms length bodies (ALBs) must embed health creation criteria into their master developments, funding distributions, and regulatory standards.
      </p>

      <img src="assets/images/feature-nature.jpeg" alt="Natural infrastructure and green spaces" style="width:100%;">

      <h2>Key partner agency alignment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Homes England:</strong> Integrating active design, walkable neighbourhoods, community hubs, and green corridors into master planning and housing delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>Active Travel England &amp; Living Streets:</strong> Designing streets and urban infrastructure that encourage walking, cycling, and natural daily movement.</li>
        <li><strong>The Wildlife Trusts &amp; Natural England:</strong> Expanding green infrastructure and accessible nature within 15 minutes of every home.</li>
        <li><strong>National Academy for Social prescribing (NASP):</strong> Connecting clinical care with non-clinical community assets, creative arts, and nature programmes.</li>
      </ul>

